; Token Exercise, version 1 (RFC 8610): the holder Instance's signed projection.issue Exercise
; that a request for an authority token carries to the realm's token endpoint (§9.9, OP-150
; m.2). It travels as the form parameter `access_exercise`, base64url (RFC 4648 §5, no padding)
; of its deterministic CBOR (RFC 8949 §4.2.1). Rules this file does not define are those of
; kernel.cddl.
;
; The request beside it names the same authority: `authorization_details` (RFC 9396) has one
; detail per bounds action, or one `intent` detail whose `intent` is the digest of `target`;
; each detail's `type` is "<namespace>:<name>:<major>" and `schema` the Action Schema digest in
; text form ("sha-256:" base64url). `resource` (RFC 8707) is one member of the payload's
; `audience`. The AIS is a COSE_Sign1 by the holder Instance's key over an
; actor-intent-statement whose `pep` is the realm's issuer; that key is the request's DPoP key,
; so the token's `cnf.jkt` is the actor Instance's KeyBinding (§9.9.4). A refresh carries a new
; Exercise: every refresh is a new decision (§9.9.3 rule 6).

token-exercise = {
  domain: domain-id,                  ; the realm's governing domain
  nonce: bstr .size (16..64),
  intent: intent-envelope,            ; access/projection_issue, opaque.payload = digest of payload
  payload: bstr,                      ; meta-payload { projection_issue: … }, deterministic CBOR
  basis: exercise-basis,
  capacity: capacity,
  ais: bstr,                          ; COSE_Sign1, application/access-ais+cbor
  ? target: intent-envelope,          ; the one intent of an exact-intent token
}
